"On the diameter of Schrijver graphs - arXiv Combinatorics (https://arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/paper/2112.01884v2)\nciteturn4search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.9 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; DOI: 10.1016/j.dam.2024.02.019 ... In this paper, we compute the diameter of the graph $\\operatorname{SG}(2k+r,k)$ with $r \\geq 1$.\n\n## On the diameter of Schrijver graphs\n\nAgustina Victoria Ledezma, Adrián Pastine, Pablo Torres, Mario Valencia-Pabon\n\nPublished: 2021-12-03 | Updated: 2022-02-11\n\nNote:\n\nDOI: 10.1016/j.dam.2024.02.019\n\nchromatic number graph kneser\n\n### Abstract\n\nFor $k \\geq 1$ and $n \\geq 2k$, the well known Kneser graph $\\operatorname{KG}(n,k)$ has all $k$-element subsets of an $n$-element set as vertices; two such subsets are adjacent if they are disjoint. Schrijver constructed a vertex-critical subgraph $\\operatorname{SG}(n,k)$ of $\\operatorname{KG}(n,k)$ with the same chromatic number. In this paper, we compute the diameter of the graph $\\operatorname{SG}(2k+r,k)$ with $r \\geq 1$. We obtain an exact value of the diameter of $\\operatorname{SG}(2k+r,k)$ when $r \\in \\{1,2\\}$ or when $r \\geq k-3$. For the remained cases, when $3 \\leq r \\leq k-4$, we obtain that the diameter of $\\operatorname{SG}(2k+r,k)$ belongs to the integer interval $[4..k-r-1]$.\n\nMaintained by Per Alexandersson, per@symmetricfunctions.com--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe e-positivity and Schur positivity of some spiders and broom trees (2023) | David G. L. Wang | 2 Citations (https://scispace.com/papers/the-e-positivity-and-schur-positivity-of-some-spiders-and-emnge9i3)\nciteturn4search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.8 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; Journal Article 10.1016/j.dam.2022.10.012 ... PDF\n\nJournal Article10.1016/j.dam.2022.10.012\n\n# The e-positivity and Schur positivity of some spiders and broom trees\n\nDavid G. L. Wang,Monica M. Y. Wang +1 more\n\n- 01 Jan 2023\n\n - Discrete 